         "{", "i1", ",", " ", "i2", ",", " ", "i3", ",", " ", "i4", "}",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "."}], "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{"An absent amplitude returns ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"0"}]],
      "InlineFormula"],
     ". That is the same missing-amplitude convention used by ",
     ButtonBox["FactorizationAmplitudeChannels", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/FactorizationAmplitudeChannels"],
     ". For an entire calculation, prefer that function or ",
     ButtonBox["ConstructAmplitude", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ConstructAmplitude"], ", which also \
carry the channel and external-state information needed for sewing and \
validation."}], "Notes"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT if needed", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Skip this setup if HEPCAT is already loaded. These examples assume \
